I've been banging my head against the wall with this error. It appears that returning `void` like the documentation shows is causing the error. When returning `void`, Vite will chunk synchronous modules with asynchronous modules, causing the chunk to be preloaded. If you return a default value to catch everything else, then Vite will __not__ do this. Thankfully, that default return value will still pass over asynchronous components you define with `defineAsyncComponent`, but it will catch everything else, possibly causing large builds. There may be a work around, I'm still playing with a solution.

