That's because `navigator.userAgent.includes('Mobile')` invokes a global API (when you declare `const bar`) that Rollup doesn't know if it causes side effects. For example, maybe the API changes the state of the page or assigns a global variable somewhere else.

In this case, it's obvious that there's no side effects, but Rollup doesn't keep a [complete catalog of the global APIs](https://github.com/rollup/rollup/blob/a2744ea5b3a3cd2c21c7d5c7905412b0536b19e6/src/ast/nodes/shared/knownGlobals.ts#L152) to know if it has no side effects or not. In this case, you need to use a [`/*@__PURE__*/` annotation](https://rollupjs.org/configuration-options/#pure) to signal to Rollup that it has no side effects.

So try changing your code to something like this and the code should no longer be bundled:
```js
export const bar = {
  disabled: /*@__PURE__*/ navigator.userAgent.includes('Mobile'),
};
```

