To trigger a style update when modifying scss files, I've managed to change the main style file to .css (eg: `sass/index.css`) and use the regular `@import` to include any additional .scss file . Eg:
* Rename to `sass/index.css`
```css
@import 'tailwindcss';

@import 'components/_simple-test.scss';
```
* Modify main.js to import the .css file instead 
```javascript
import '../sass/index.css';
```

After this change, any change in .scss files imported in the main .css file triggers an automatic update. However, nested .scss file imports using `@use` inside .scss files do not trigger the CSS update unless the main scss file is updated, so this is a partial solution. If you import all the .scss files inside the main .css file, the update will be triggered accordingly.

