### 💡 Suggestions

To improve developer experience and avoid this subtle platform-specific issue:

- **Vite could default to:**
  ```ts
  root: fs.realpathSync.native(path.resolve('./'))
  ```
  This would ensure `config.root` matches the internally resolved paths from the start, avoiding volume mismatches on Windows.

- **Alternatively**, document this clearly in the **Getting Started guide**, not just in Troubleshooting. For example:
  > ⚠️ On Windows, using subst drives or symlinks across volumes may cause path resolution issues. To avoid this, set `root` to `fs.realpathSync.native(path.resolve('./'))`.

- **Long-term**, consider centralizing all path resolution logic into a dedicated utility or plugin. A project like [`upath`](https://github.com/anodynos/upath) could serve as inspiration — it provides consistent cross-platform path normalization and could help avoid subtle differences across Vite’s internal plugins.

Even though this behavior is documented, it’s a real-world pitfall that developers can easily run into — and spend hours debugging. Centralizing path handling or improving defaults would make Vite more predictable and easier to maintain across platforms.

