Hey! I recently also built a small Vite plugin that helps with handling dynamic import maps, especially when the import map needs to be created asynchronously (like fetching it dynamically from a server).

For your usecase where the importmap seems to be known at buildtime and can be loaded synchonously, this plugin might not add much benefit (actually it worsens the performance a bit - be aware!). However I thought to share it within this discussion anyways, just in case it’s helpful for others who might run into a similar situation :)

https://www.npmjs.com/package/vite-plugin-dynamic-importmap

Example:

Store your importmap in `public/importmap.json` so that Vite makes the file accessible on the webserver.
Then adjust your vite config as follows:

```typescript
// vite.config.ts
import dynamicImportmap from "vite-plugin-dynamic-importmap";

export default {
  plugins: [dynamicImportmap({ importmap: "/importmap.json" })],
};
```

The plugin first removes all scripts from your index.html, then fetch the importmap asynchronously and insert it to the DOM and then re-adds the previously removed scripts back to the DOM again.

