For standard build, you should be able to configure [`build.rollupOptions`](https://vitejs.dev/config/build-options.html#build-rollupoptions) using [`external`](https://rollupjs.org/configuration-options/#external) and [`output.globals`](https://rollupjs.org/configuration-options/#output-globals)

e.g.:
```js
const globals = {
  react: 'React',
  'react-dom': 'ReactDOM',
};

export default defineConfig({
  // ...
  build: {
    rollupOptions: {
      external: Object.keys(globals), // ['react', 'react-dom']
      output: {
        format: 'iife',
        name: 'MyBundle',
        globals,
      },
    },
  },
});
```

This doesn't apply to Vite in `serve` mode (i.e. local dev), for non-ESM bundles. For that, I tried various plugins, but found [`vite-plugin-external`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/vite-plugin-external) did exactly what I needed. I use it like this:


```js
import createExternal from 'vite-plugin-external';

const globals = {
  react: 'React',
  'react-dom': 'ReactDOM',
};

export default defineConfig(({command}) => {
  return {
    // ...
    plugins: [
      // ... other plugins

      // only add this in dev server mode
      ...(command === 'serve' ? [createExternal({externals: globals})] : []),
    ],
    build: {
      // ... same build config as above, though `external`/`globals` from that don't actually apply in dev server
    }
  };
});
```

