The error of "require is not defined" is happening because Vite does not support processing CJS modules. By externalizing the module, it should work. But it seems resolving by Vite + externalizing the module (returning `{ id: resolveId, external: true }` in resolveId hook) does not work. Probably this is related to #19461.

As a workaround you can change the virtual module to be a facade module by tweaking the plugin to be like:
```js
const p = {
  name: 'server-only-module',
  async resolveId(id, importer, {ssr}) {
    const prefix = 'server-only:';

    if (id.startsWith(prefix)) {
      if (ssr) return id
      return '\0empty-module';
    }
  },
  load(id) {
    if (id === '\0empty-module') return 'export {}';
    const prefix = 'server-only:';
    if (id.startsWith(prefix)) {
      return `export * from ${JSON.stringify(id.slice(prefix.length))}`
    }
  },
}
```

