## Solution for Starting Vite on Multiple Hosts

We implemented a feature allowing the Vite development server to be accessed through multiple custom domain names. Here's the generic solution:

### 1. Basic Configuration

```typescript
import { defineConfig, type Plugin } from "vite";

export default defineConfig(() => {
  return {
    server: {
      port: 3000,
      // Bind to all network interfaces, allowing access from any hostname
      host: "0.0.0.0",
      // List of allowed hostnames
      allowedHosts: [
        "custom-domain1.example.com",
        "custom-domain2.example.com",
      ],
      hmr: true,
    },
    plugins: [
      // Custom print plugin and other plugins
    ],
  };
});
```

### 2. Custom Plugin for Improved URL Display

```typescript
const printUrls = (): Plugin => {
  return {
    name: "custom-domains-logger",
    configureServer(server) {
      server.printUrls = () => {
        const greenArrow = "\x1b[32m➜\x1b[0m"; // Green arrow
        const allowedHosts =
          "allowedHosts" in server.config.server
            ? (server.config.server.allowedHosts as string[])
            : [];
        const port = server.config.server?.port || 3000;

        if (allowedHosts.length > 0) {
          console.log("");
          allowedHosts.forEach((host: string) => {
            // Customize labels based on domain characteristics
            const label = host.includes("domain1") ? "Environment 1" : "Environment 2";
            console.log(
              `  ${greenArrow}  ${label}:\thttp://${host}:${port}/`,
            );
          });
        }
      };
    },
  };
};
```

### 3. Output Result

When the server starts, it will display:

```
  ➜  Environment 1:  http://custom-domain1.example.com:3000/
  ➜  Environment 2:  http://custom-domain2.example.com:3000/
```

The arrow (➜) is green, improving visibility.

### Key Points

1. `host: "0.0.0.0"` ensures binding to all network interfaces
2. `allowedHosts` lists all domain names that need access, preventing CORS issues
3. Custom plugin overrides the `server.printUrls()` method to improve CLI output

Make sure these domains are correctly mapped to your local IP address in your hosts file:

```
127.0.0.1 custom-domain1.example.com
127.0.0.1 custom-domain2.example.com
```

This enables access to the same Vite server from multiple custom domain names.

