And this shows that this isn't a tree-shaking issue, but rather that the `.then()` chain is misplaced when `__vitePreload()` is injected:

Compiled _foo.js_:
```js
const foo = {
  bar: 123
};
export {
  foo
};
```

Compiled _index.js_:
```js
import { __vitePreload } from "../_virtual/preload-helper-DAnU8ViX.js";
(async () => {
  const { bar } = await __vitePreload(async () => {
    const { bar: bar2 } = await import("./foo-Wx1xxurL.js");
    return { bar: bar2 };
  }, true ? [] : void 0).then((a) => a.foo);
  console.log(bar);
})();
```

The `.then((a) => a.foo)` should remain right after `import()`, but instead, it's moved to the end of `__vitePreload()`. I think this is coming from https://github.com/vitejs/vite/blob/998303b438734e8219715fe6883b97fb10404c16/packages/vite/src/node/plugins/importAnalysisBuild.ts#L348-L351

