@bluwy Sounds like they want to opt out of sync style loading altogether?

> Vite already hoists the styles needed for a HTML in the head (which should be requested/streamed very early)

Requests start early, but even then, the doc will only render once all styles that are linked this way are fully loaded. If *all* styles are injected as preloads, you can control at which point you want to make the page visible. For example:

```html
<html data-loaded="false">
<head>
  <link rel="preload" href="x" as="style" />
  <link rel="preload" href="y" as="style" />
  <link rel="preload" href="z" as="style" />
  <script>
    // Don't wait for styles if connection is slow
    if (navigator.connection?.effectiveType?.includes('2g')) {
      document.documentElement.dataset.loaded = true
    }

    // Don't wait for styles for longer than than 3.5s
    setTimeout(() => (document.documentElement.dataset.loaded = true), 3500)

    const stylePreloads = document.querySelectorAll('link[rel="preload"][as="style"]')
    let loadedCount = 0
    for (const preload of stylePreloads) {
      preload.onload = () => {
        preload.onload = null
        preload.rel = 'stylesheet'
        if (++loadedCount === stylePreloads.length) {
          document.documentElement.dataset.loaded = true
        }
      }
    }
  </script>
  <style>
    [data-loaded="false"] body > * { display: none; }
    [data-loaded="false"] body::before{ content: 'Loading, please wait...' }
  </style>
</head>
```

